Online Office Docker builds

This directory contains the supported source-build pipeline for the Online Office Debian OCI
image. The pipeline builds the document engine and server from source and publishes the resulting
image as ghcr.io/kreoh/online-office.

The proven Jenkins route uses:

* from-source/Builder.Dockerfile for the Debian build environment
* from-source/build.sh for the pinned source build
* from-source/Debian for the final runtime image
* from-source/debrand.py for source and runtime debranding checks

The build requires an exact 40-character source revision. Jenkins supplies the repository, branch,
revision, cache and image name through the ONLINE_OFFICE_SOURCE_* variables documented in
from-source/build.sh.

The source build keeps the established technical coolwsd executable and /cool routes for protocol
compatibility. Product identity, container metadata and installed user-facing content use Online
Office.

Native builds and tests run only in Jenkins. Build authorisation does not authorise
publication or deployment. Local inspection and checks that do not compile are permitted.

Upstream also supplies a separate from-packages build, image SBOM aggregation and
publication tooling under from-packages/scripts. Its base-image, optional Python,
platform and signing choices do not replace this distribution's source pipeline.
See ../SBOM.md for the upstream SBOM format and scan limitations. The source pipeline
retains its immutable-rootfs scan and validates its neutral SPDX 3.0.1 document name.
